{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nPass 1 (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py`, `passes.pass1_chunk`, prompts `reviewers/plan_review_finder.md` + one `plan_review_<ID>.md` per criterion, routing in `criteria_routing.json`, frontier class = Opus on Bedrock) is the expensive pass. A criterion edit cannot be judged from stored data alone, so Tier 2 re-runs finders on a small fixed sample. Per-criterion edits are far cheaper in single-criterion mode; prior work (`docs/experiments/plan-review-model-tradeoff.md`) showed Opus is flat to 12 criteria/turn while Sonnet degrades.\n\n**Execution tier is per-criterion — exact contract.** `registry.exec_tier(crit)` (registry.py:604-610) returns ONLY one of `\"AGENT\"` / `\"2-STEP\"` / `\"1-TURN\"` — there is NO `\"CONTAINER\"` return value. It returns `\"AGENT\"` for any id in `AGENT_TIER` (registry.py:97-116 — the FULL frozenset: `G1G2, E4, A1, G6, G3, G4, G7, T1, T3, T5c, T8, T10, T11, asserted-capability, evidence-kind, decomp-shape`) or when `crit[\"exec\"] == \"AGENT\"`. `G3`/`G4` therefore resolve to `\"AGENT\"` from `exec_tier`, NOT a container value — the container fan-out (`pass1_container`) is a SEPARATE downstream step: `production_batch_runner._resolve_criteria` (production_batch_runner.py:198-248) splits criteria into `(single, agent, skipped)` purely by `exec_tier(desc) == \"AGENT\"`, and its own docstring states G3/G4 are \"pulled out of `agent` by `run_pass1` itself\" — i.e. `run_pass1` inspects the resolved `agent` list afterward and routes G3/G4 to `pass1_container` from there. Tier-2 derives its own single/agent/container split the same way: resolve via `exec_tier`, then separately check membership in the (small, hardcoded in `run_pass1`) G3/G4 container set.\n\n**Single-criterion filtering — exact mechanism.** `BatchRunRequest.criteria` (workflow/runners.py:66, `tuple[Mapping[str, Any], ...]`, each entry `{prompt, with?}`) is what `_resolve_criteria` actually filters on. `req.with_inputs[\"probe_criteria\"]` (a SEPARATE field) is consumed ONLY by `_project_criteria` for `project.*`-prefixed fan-in criteria (production_batch_runner.py:114-118) — it does NOT filter `req.criteria`/`_resolve_criteria`'s built-in dispatch. To run exactly one named criterion against `ProductionBatchRunner` directly, Tier-2 constructs `req.criteria = ({\"prompt\": f\"plan-review-{id}\"},)` (a single-entry tuple) itself — `_resolve_criteria` then correctly routes that one descriptor through `exec_tier` into `single` or `agent`. (The workflow-level PROBE MODE that reads `ctx.inputs[\"probe_criteria\"]` to filter built-ins, `workflow_ops.py:254-263`, is a different, higher-layer mechanism for workflow-driven runs and is not used here since Tier-2 invokes the runner directly.)\n\nCost varies by resolved tier: `1-TURN`/`2-STEP` criteria cost ≈ $0.17-0.25/sample (the AC's ceiling, applies ONLY to ids resolving to `1-TURN`/`2-STEP`); `AGENT`-tier criteria (including the G3/G4 container subset) cost their real production rate and are reported separately in the ledger, with no fixed per-sample ceiling assumed.\n\n**Tier-1 chaining, corrected.** `tier1.replay_review` requires a STORED `verification` on each finding to build `stored_answers` — a freshly-generated Tier-2 candidate finding has none, so Tier-1's `per_question_agreement`/`distribution_shift` cannot run on it directly. Tier 2's \"downstream\" instead reuses Tier-1/Tier-0's COMPUTATION functions: candidate findings are verified fresh via the SAME `verify_findings` seam Tier-1 uses, then `review_kernel.decide.pass3_decide`/`pass3_over_findings` computes a CANDIDATE VERDICT from them, compared against the STORED verdict already recorded in the original review's sidecar — a verdict-level flip matrix (Tier-0's shape), not a per-question agreement table.\n\n## Approach\n\nBuild `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier2.py`:\n\n- **Fixed sample**: ~20 review ids drawn once by the Tier-1 stratified sampler (additional strata: ≥5 containers, ≥8 with ≥10 findings, ≥3 from the LMN store), committed as `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/tier2-sample.json`. Plan text from reconstructed material; code-grounded AGENT criteria run against the pinned `verified_at_sha` snapshot via `source=attested`.\n- **Full mode**: run the candidate registry/prompts through `ProductionBatchRunner`, frontier class pinned to Bedrock Opus; compare candidate Pass-1 finding sets to stored findings by `norm_id` (Jaccard, gained/lost per criterion); verify candidate findings via `verify_findings`, compute their verdict via `pass3_decide`/`pass3_over_findings`, compare to the stored verdict (flip matrix).\n- **Single-criterion mode**: `--criteria T5c` constructs `req.criteria = ({\"prompt\": \"plan-review-T5c\"},)` on a `BatchRunRequest` and runs it directly through `ProductionBatchRunner`/`_resolve_criteria` (real single/agent dispatch by `exec_tier`, with G3/G4's container split applied same as `run_pass1`) over the sample; compares only that criterion's findings.\n- Baseline for a criterion whose stored findings predate the current `regver`: a one-time baseline run recorded in the ledger; otherwise stored findings are the baseline.\n- Budget pre-flight from stored per-criterion usage (`coverage.usage.per_criterion`) × current price.\n\n`src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/__main__.py`: add a `tier2` subparser (`--candidate <registry-dir>`, `--criteria <id>`, plus shared `--store`/`--cache-dir`/`--out-dir`) and a `_run_tier2` dispatch branch, mirroring `tier0`/`tier1`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier2.py` (new)\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/__main__.py` (edited — `tier2` subparser + dispatch)\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/tier2-sample.json`, `tier2-*.md` (new/generated)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier2.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: with a `FakeRunner` returning canned `P1Output`, gained/lost findings per criterion match expectations; single-criterion mode for a `1-TURN` id (`req.criteria` single-entry) issues exactly one chunk per sampled review; single-criterion mode for an `AGENT`-tier id (e.g. `T5c`) dispatches agentically via `ProductionBatchRunner`'s `agent` bucket, NOT forced single-turn; G3/G4 route to the container path the same way `run_pass1` does; a run is refused when the frontier model is not the Bedrock Opus id; the sample file is validated against the corpus manifest; a candidate finding set is verified via `verify_findings` and its verdict computed via `pass3_decide`, compared correctly against a fixture's stored verdict. Live (commissioning, ≤$60): one full-mode baseline over the fixed sample. `__main__.py`'s `tier2` subcommand dispatches correctly.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A committed fixed sample of review ids exists with the strata above; checked by the sample file and manifest cross-check.\n- [x] `tier2 --candidate <registry-dir>` produces finding-set Jaccard and gained/lost-per-criterion tables plus a candidate-vs-stored verdict flip matrix; checked by one generated report.\n- [x] `tier2 --criteria <1-TURN-or-2-STEP-id>` costs ≤ N × $0.25 in the ledger; checked by the ledger. An AGENT-tier `--criteria` run (including G3/G4) is priced at its real production rate and reported separately, with no fixed per-sample ceiling assumed.\n- [x] Commissioning spend for this ticket ≤ $60 and every call uses the Bedrock frontier model id; checked by the ledger.\n- [x] Unit tests pass in `make test`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788239386738947001,"uuid":"349cddb8-e5e9-416b-a7e3-473348db09f9"}